            </section>

            <section id="clinic-questions">
              <h2>10. Analytical Questions &amp; Observations</h2>
              <ul>
                <li>Which weekdays and hours have relatively high patient-entry activity? The patient-count heatmap and KDE are designed to expose the distribution across those dimensions.</li>
                <li>How does the notebook's calculated financial total vary by weekday and entry hour? The grouped sum and revenue heatmap support comparison, with the financial-total caveat above.</li>
                <li>How does the row-level Total Revenue distribution differ across weekdays? The boxplot and violin plot offer complementary distribution views.</li>
                <li>How can Financial Class and Doctor Type be used to explore clinic activity? The report pages organize views around those categories, but further interpretation depends on their exact filter and KPI definitions.</li>
                <li>How can heatmaps and density plots reveal patterns that summary cards do not show? They reveal how activity is distributed across weekday/hour combinations rather than only showing a top-level number.</li>
              </ul>
              <p>These are exploratory questions, not established operational findings. The supplied notebook and screenshots do not prove staffing shortages, doctor productivity differences, patient waiting times, profitability, operational efficiency or cost savings.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="clinic-limitations">
              <h2>11. Limitations &amp; Data-Quality Considerations</h2>
              <ul>
                <li><code>fillna(0)</code> is applied to the entire DataFrame, so missing non-financial values are also replaced with zero. The notebook does not validate this assumption against the source system.</li>
                <li>The financial cleaning function strips hyphens and other characters. Its behaviour should be checked against the source conventions; for example, it does not distinguish an em dash from a negative sign through a documented rule.</li>
                <li>The supplied notebook does not demonstrate a formal duplicate-record investigation or a formal outlier investigation.</li>
                <li>No verified waiting-time, consultation-duration, doctor-productivity or profitability calculation is shown.</li>
                <li>The notebook's Total Revenue formula adds Lab Cost to two fields named as revenue. Its output is therefore a calculated sum of the three fields, not demonstrated profit or net income.</li>
                <li>The dashboard screenshots do not establish the exact definition of each KPI card. The displayed values vary by view/filter context and are not safe to combine without checking the PBIX calculations.</li>
                <li>The project does not establish that missing values, duplicates or all other data-quality issues were fully resolved.</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

